  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Information Technology obligated $3.5B in federal contracts in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Information Technology won 840 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.1M. General Dynamics Information Technology's obligations are down 25.2% year over year. Department of Defense is the largest buyer of General Dynamics Information Technology this year, obligating $1.1B, followed by the General Services Administration at $759M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $750M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for General Dynamics Information Technology at $1.6B, supported by Custom Computer Programming Services at $611M and Engineering Services at $451M. Historical context shows variability: obligations ranged from $2.4B in FY21 up to $4.8B in FY24 before falling to $3.5B in FY26. This picture shows a company with concentrated technical services work and a heavy reliance on a few large federal buyers during the fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of General Dynamics Information Technology?",
        "body": "Department of Defense obligated $1.1B to General Dynamics Information Technology in FY2026 to date. General Services Administration obligated $759M and Department of Health and Human Services obligated $750M. Other notable buyers include Department of Veterans Affairs at $162M, Department of State at $137M, and Department of the Interior at $136M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the primary services and markets for General Dynamics Information Technology?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market for General Dynamics Information Technology at $1.6B in FY2026 to date. Custom Computer Programming Services contributed $611M and Engineering Services contributed $451M. General Dynamics Information Technology also performed work classified as Other Computer Related Services at $185M and Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $158M."
      }
    ]
  },
